WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.140
Could the future of renewable energy

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.480
lie with a common household chemical?

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.620
Ammonia might power your cleaning products

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.000
and fertilize your plants, but it could soon

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.920
be the carrier for moving energy around the world.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.860
Oil and gas, which make up most of our energy supply,

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.440
can easily be shipped and stored.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.440
But renewable energy, which travels through

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.320
the power grid as electricity, can’t, preventing it

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.160
from becoming a bigger player on the world market.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.180
That’s why researchers are trying to convert

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.440
solar and wind energy into liquid ammonia,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.200
which would allow renewables to be stored

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.240
and shipped as easily as petroleum products.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.080
But the current process of creating ammonia

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.340
is anything but green.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.980
Combining nitrogen molecules,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.880
which are pulled from the air, and hydrogen molecules,

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.100
which come from either natural gas or coal,

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.380
creates massive amounts of greenhouse gases,

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.400
some 1% of CO2 emissions worldwide.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.360
To make truly green ammonia, scientists get their

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.600
hydrogen from water by separating

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.940
it from oxygen atoms using electricity.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.000
And electricity is what renewables do best.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.100
That means regions with lots of wind and sun,

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.940
like Australia, are ground zero for the new

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.060
kind of ammonia production.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.460
There, the world’s biggest producer of ammonia

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.460
is building a pilot plant that

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.000
would rely on solar electricity.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.420
The new plant will feed power from a solar array

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.680
into a bank of electrolyzers, which

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.960
will convert water into hydrogen.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.160
This won’t produce fully green ammonia because

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.320
natural gas will still be used in other parts of the plant.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.700
But it’s a critical first step --

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.620
generating hydrogen accounts for half of the CO2

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.880
emissions from a standard ammonia production plant.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.480
To succeed in creating truly “green” ammonia,

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.840
the industry will have to do away with hybrid

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.800
or conventional plants altogether and, instead,

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.820
rely on electrochemical cells.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.160
These cells use electricity and catalysts

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.720
to knit components of air and water into ammonia,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.200
all without the heat and pressure

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.920
normally used to make the chemical.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.140
This isn’t easy - at normal temperaturesand pressures,

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.899
you can produce ammonia quickly or efficiently.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:11.900
But not both.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.700
Now, researchers are trying to create

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.240
a single cell that does it all.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.480
Even if they can do it, many challenges remain.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.860
For example, scientists still need to figure out

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.180
the best way to extract energy from

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.160
liquid ammonia once it arrives at its destination.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.360
But if they can pull it off, this new technology

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.100
could be the key to sustainable energy--

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.860
all without carbon.

